    "title": "Cooking up success at TLCA - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By David Davis ,\n24 minutes ago\nSAN ANGELO, Texas ( Concho Valley Homepage ) — Students at TLCA seem to be learning lessons that go far beyond the classroom.\nThe school offers a culinary arts program designed to give students hands-on experience in the kitchen.\nTLCA’s Culinary Arts teacher, Elizabeth Sides, says that she began teaching the course back in 2018, but it hit a snag in 2020 due to COVID-19. However, the course got cooking again last year and is now rustling up more culinary students.\nThe school principal, Dr. Sarah Grace Hernandez, says the course is meant to provide skills that students at TLCA can use later in life. “The biggest thing I think… The takeaway for this program is we want our students to have fun learning and be able to have experiences that they can transfer and take with them into their adulthood”, said Dr. Hernandez.\nThe class is already giving TLCA Junior, Axel Eledezma, a solid foundation for future goals. Eledezma said, “I think it’ll be good because I want to be in college, so I think it’ll be good to be able to know how to cook for myself or for buddies that I might have. Also. I want to be a dad too. So I want to learn how to cook and have my kids experience the same things that I got to experience…when I was young.”\nThe program offers students not only a form of creative expression, but also gives TLCA students a taste of the Culinary Career world if they choose to pursue it.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ConchoValleyHomepage.com.",
